  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(x)=\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} x$ and $g(x)=\\frac{x^4-2 x^3+3 x^2-2 x+2}{2 x^2-2 x+1}$. Then the domain of $f \\circ g$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gvyeA",
      "text": "$[0, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HAnJy",
      "text": "$[1, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "srpCg",
      "text": "$(0, \\infty)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8pebX",
      "text": "$\\mathbb{R}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(g(x))=\\ln \\left(\\frac{x^4-2 x^3+3 x^2-2 x+2}{2 x^2-2 x+1}\\right)$\n\nSince $2 x^2-2 x+1>0 \\quad \\forall x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\because(-2)^2-4(2) < 0$\nConsider\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& x^4-2 x^3+3 x^2-2 x+2 \\\\\n& =\\left(x^4-2 x^3+x^2\\right)+\\left(x^2-2 x+1\\right)+\\left(1+x^2\\right) \\\\\n& =x^2(x-1)^2+(x-1)^2+\\left(x^2+1\\right)>0 \\forall x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow g(x)>0 \\forall x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\ln f((x)), f(x)>0 \\forall x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow x \\in \\mathbb{R} \\text { is domain }\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
